      "side": 1,
      "message": "In Android, we very often have:\n\n```\nANDROID: GKI: blah\n```\n\nFor upstream, I\u0027ve no idea.\n\nIf this were a driver or subtree named \"cfi\", then lowercase would make sense.\n\nI suppose the files are `include/linux/cfi.h`, `kernel/cfi.c` etc. so it make *some* sense. But the change has nothing to do with those files directly. The banners in those files say CFI.\n\n---\n\n```shell\n$ git log --oneline | grep -wc CFI\n154\n$ git log --oneline | grep -wc cfi\n72\n$ git log --oneline | grep -wc CFI:\n5\n$ git log --oneline | grep -wc cfi:\n46\n```",
